							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">From what I&#039;ve seen, hip hop is a huge part of the Filipino youth culture... the 25-35&#039;s sure do love their Stevie B and Johnny O though&nbsp; <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/grin.gif" alt="Grin" border="0" /> so it&#039;s obvious why they might want to keep tabs on a group with a pinoy frontman that has a good deal of influence amongst local like minded youths.&nbsp; <br /><br />The relationship the US has had with The Phillipines isn&#039;t exactly great.&nbsp; The country has been on the do not travel list since 9/11 if I remember correctly, not to mention we (USA) owned the damn place for almost 40 years... the country itself is interesting because the western influence is evident from the popular religions to small cultural nuances, but since the country has only had an official constitution for &gt;20 years and the avg person makes such little money, a situation like what happened recently in Thailand isn&#039;t out of the question.&nbsp; The place is a hot bed for political dissent/revolution, and whether or not this could directly effect us as citizens in regards to our SAFETY, I&#039;m not so sure about. <br /><br />I feel that they are keeping tabs on what is going on over in the phillipines, just to protect fiscal interests... maybe they are in the process of staging a coup *shrug*<br /><br />Geo is right though, oldest trick in the book... a lot of those have been in use for the last 5 years<br /><br />Im tired and rambling, dont mind me&nbsp; <img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Smileys/default/grin.gif" alt="Grin" border="0" /><br /><br />who wouldve thought that the &quot;New World Order&quot; would be brought upon by the party whose flagship *until 2001* was to minimalize govt. involvement.&nbsp; You can keep your assault weapons until we throw you into secret detention centers...<br /><br />this is disgusting&nbsp; </div>
